      "required": true,
      "default_value_repr": "",
      "constraints": "Exact version-1 envelope with training, scoring, prediction, initialization and config. Config requires integer seed in [0,2**32); optional variant v43/v47, positive integer batch_size, nonnegative integer num_workers and integer epoch_limit in [1,35]. Qualification uses explicit batch_size=1, num_workers=0 and epoch_limit=1. Finite float32-compatible arrays shaped (4,3,256,256), with caller-defined ordered times and the source thermal-channel physical scale. False color is 1-((channel2-channel1+4)/6, (channel1-channel0+4)/9, (channel1-243)/60), without clipping or per-image normalization. At least ten ordered training examples and nonempty scoring/prediction populations. Training/scoring supply label and annotation_mean arrays shaped (1,256,256) in [0,1]. Globally distinct nonempty keys; source shuffled ten-fold selection and explicit v43/v47 branch-fold subsets. Explicit seed and initialization policy: random, supplied encoder states or supplied full-model states per selected fold. Complete MaxViT/U-Net models, source loss/schedule, terminal checkpoints and all selected folds. Optional epoch_limit explicitly shortens the schedule."
    },
    {
      "direction": "output",
      "name": "result",
      "type_desc": "dict",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "required": true,
      "default_value_repr": "",
      "constraints": "Ordered per-example (1,256,256) unnormalized weighted fold/branch sums, plus column-major one-based run-length masks using strict threshold0.5 and the empty marker \"-\". Return variant, seed, initialization, epoch limit and per-fold optimizer-update summaries. The field named probabilities is a source-weighted sum that can exceed one; it is not a calibrated posterior. Diagnostic threshold sweeps do not replace the fixed final threshold. No trained model is returned for later reuse."
    }
